  "description": "OpenOmicsBench provides traceable offline benchmarks for RNA-seq, DNA and protein sequences, single-cell labels, genomic intervals and synthetic read-level taxonomy. Version 14 includes 16 biological bulk RNA-seq objects from 11 Expression Atlas studies, checked compact and full input packs, sample and contrast validation, descriptive RNA-seq QC, and agreement checks against declared DESeq2 reference analyses. It also includes a six-assay demo, verifiable reports and a searchable catalog of 25 objects. Reference agreement does not establish biological ground truth; synthetic fixtures test software behavior only.",
